The initial population of SO is generated by a random uniform distribution which may result in the initial snakes being located far from the optimal point, leading to inadequate optimization ability of the algorithm58. Sobol sequences are a kind of low-discrepancy sequence that is widely employed in optimization problems and numerical simulations. In order to ensure that the search space is thoroughly searched, especially in high-dimensional issues, these sequences are made to generate points that are uniformly scattered throughout a multidimensional space59. This technique guarantees that the starting population is evenly distributed throughout the search space, laying a foundation for the optimization algorithm’s exploration and exploitation stages. Sobol sequences enhance the algorithm’s capability to explore global optima, lower the likelihood of early convergence to suboptimal solutions, and enable a more comprehensive exploration of the problem landscape, which is why it is very beneficial for high-dimensional optimization problems60. Each snake is initialized using Eq. (23): 23\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
