Non-parametric statistical tests were utilized to statistically evaluate the efficiency differences among the compared algorithms, due to the stochastic characteristics of metaheuristic optimization approaches. The Friedman test was initially applied for a comprehensive comparison across all benchmark functions to determine the occurrence of significant efficiency differences between the algorithms and the proposed DASO. Friedman test entails sorting each block of rows collectively, and subsequently employing the ranked column values. Therefore, the mean ranks of each algorithm is evaluated and sorted62. Thereafter, pairwise comparisons were performed utilizing the Wilcoxon signed-rank test with a significance threshold of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
